+---
+id: task-001-give-each-task-a-stable-id
+type: task
+title: "Give each task a stable id"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Give each task a stable id
+
+The app needs a stable way to refer to a task, one that still works after the task is renamed.
+
+## What to build
+
+- Every task has an `id`: a string that no other task of the same list has. `add` returns the task with its `id`.
+- The task list gets `get(id)`, which returns the task with that id as a `Result<Task>`, like the list's other methods; an unknown id fails with `not-found`.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+- An id stays the same when the task is renamed, completed, reopened or tagged.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `add` returns a task with a non-empty `id`, and two tasks in one list never share an id.
+- `get(id)` returns the task added with that id; an unknown id gives `not-found`.
+- After `rename`, the task is still found by its old id, and its title is the new one.
+- Each title-taking method also works when given the id of a task.
+- Titles stay unique within a list, as before.
